<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">48 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">48 CE in world history: 4 events, 1 death and 1 state founded. 143 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a><a href="/years/42-bce">42 BCE</a><a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a><a href="/years/27-bce">27 BCE</a><a href="/years/48" aria-current="page">48 CE</a><a href="/years/69">69 CE</a><a href="/years/224">224 CE</a><a href="/years/357">357 CE</a><a href="/years/378">378 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-9">9 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Caesar defeats Pompey at Pharsalus</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s veterans routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>'s larger army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. Pompey fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he was murdered, and Caesar became master of the Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-28">28 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pompey is murdered on landing in Egypt</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fleeing after Pharsalus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> the Great was stabbed to death as he stepped ashore, on the orders of Ptolemy XIII's advisers. Caesar is said to have wept when shown his rival's head.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/split-of-the-xiongnu">Split of the Xiongnu</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The split of the Xiongnu took place in 48 CE, when the confederation divided into the Southern Xiongnu, who accepted Han client status, and the Northern Xiongnu.</p></div></li></ol></section>
